# LehroSol Code — example environment
#
# You do not need this file. The app is designed to run with ZERO configuration:
# it finds the LehroSol CLI on your PATH, uses ~/.lehro as its data home, and
# auto-discovers GGUF models in the usual places (D:\AI Models, Jan, LM Studio,
# the HuggingFace cache, ~/models, and similar).
#
# Copy to .env only if you need to override one of the defaults below.
# Every value here is read from the process environment; nothing is required.

# Absolute path to the LehroSol CLI entry script.
# Overrides PATH discovery. The app runs it with Electron's own binary via
# ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE, so a plain .js entrypoint works.
# Leave unset to resolve via PATH, then a couple of well-known install folders.
# LEHROSOL_BIN=C:\tools\lehrosol-cli\bin\lehrosol.js

# The CLI's data/state directory — vault, serve.json, config.json, engrams.
# This is the shared state home the app reads to stay in sync with the CLI.
# Default: %USERPROFILE%\.lehro   (~/.lehro)
# Point this at the same folder your CLI actually uses.
# LEHRO_HOME=C:\Users\you\.lehro

# EXTRA directory to scan for GGUF model files, in addition to the built-in
# candidates. Accepts MULTIPLE folders separated by your platform's path
# delimiter (";" on Windows, ":" elsewhere).
# Discovered folders can then be registered into the shared CLI vault from the
# Vault view.
# LEHRO_MODELS_DIR=D:\AI Models;D:\Shared Models
